# Project Vision & AI Instructions: aTrainingTracker

> **Canonical Source of Truth**: This file summarizes the project vision and points to the authoritative Agile Agentic ASPICE (AAA) governance rules in [`.agents/rules/aspice_governance.md`](.agents/rules/aspice_governance.md), [`docs/project_protocol.md`](docs/project_protocol.md), [`docs/coding_standards.md`](docs/coding_standards.md), and [`docs/design_guidelines.md`](docs/design_guidelines.md).

## 1. The Goal & Quality Pillars
The primary objective of this project is to build an **awesome, world-class, professional application** for tracking training activities:
1. **Requirement-Based Engineering**: No production code change is allowed without a corresponding requirement in `docs/requirements.md` and test case in `docs/tests.md`.
2. **Code Excellence & DRY**: Reuse shared formatters, repositories, and Compose components (`docs/coding_standards.md`).
3. **UI/UX Sophistication**: Follow the Material 3 patterns, visual parity checks, and component heuristics in `docs/design_guidelines.md`.
4. **Constructive Resistance (`Rule 1`)**: Never initiate shortcuts. If the human user requests an exception from standard process, first offer constructive resistance explaining the guardrail and risk; if confirmed, document the deviation in Jira and the deliverable.

## 2. Strategy A Branching & Unified 5-Stage Lifecycle (`Core Rules 1–8`)
1. **Strategy A Sprint Branching (`sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>`)**:
   * At Sprint-Start (`Ceremony 1`), establish `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>` from `develop`.
   * Each sprint ticket branches from `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>` as `feature/<KEY>`.
   * **One Atomic Commit per Ticket (`Core Rule 8`)**: Do not commit during Stages 1–4. At the end of Stage 5, squash-merge `feature/<KEY>` onto `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>` as **strictly one atomic commit** (`git merge --squash feature/<KEY> && git commit -m "<KEY>: <Summary>" && git branch -D feature/<KEY>`).
   * At Sprint-End (`Ceremony 2`), after human review and the Sprint Retrospective, merge `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>` into `develop` (`--no-ff`), delete the local branch, and tag `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>`.
2. **Epic-Scoped Persistent `pro` / `flash` Ping-Pong Subagents (`Core Rule 7`)**:
   * Maintain a persistent `(subagent_pro, subagent_flash)` pair per Parent Epic (or standalone ticket), pre-warming `subagent_flash` concurrently during Stage 1 (`Rule 63`) and rotating pairs after every 3 completed tickets (`Rule 62`).
   * Alternate Doing (`--as agent1 submit-stage`) and Gate Review (`--as agent2 gate-verdict`) across Stages 1–5 with fused Gate-to-Next-Stage turns (`Rule 60`):
     * **Stage 1 (`[Analysis]`)**: `subagent_pro` (Doing) $\rightarrow$ `subagent_flash` (Gate 1 + fused Stage 2 Doing)
     * **Stage 2 (`[Req & Test Spec]`)**: `subagent_flash` (Doing) $\rightarrow$ `subagent_pro` (Gate 2 + fused Stage 3 Doing)
     * **Stage 3 (`[Impl-Plan]`)**: `subagent_pro` (Doing) $\rightarrow$ `subagent_flash` (Gate 3 + fused Standard Stage 4 Doing)
     * **Stage 4 (`[Implementation]`)**: Verify `python3 tools/jira_util.py check-gate <Impl-Plan-Subtask-Key>` (`Core Rule 4`) before editing production code. `subagent_flash` (Standard) / `subagent_pro` (High-Risk) $\rightarrow$ opposite tier (Gate 4).
     * **Stage 5 (`[Test]`)**: `subagent_flash` (Doing) $\rightarrow$ `subagent_pro` (Gate 5 + squash-merge onto `sprint/<SPRINT_NAME>`).
3. **Two-Tier Unit Test Strategy (`Rule 60 & Rule 66`)**:
   * **Tier 1 (Per-Ticket in Stages 4 & 5)**: Run targeted package/contract unit tests (`./gradlew testDebugUnitTest --tests "com.atrainingtracker.<modified_package>.*" --tests "com.atrainingtracker.trainingtracker.build.*"`, plus `ThemeColorCentralizationAuditTest` for UI and `TranslationParityTest` for strings — never pass `--rerun-tasks`). State the exact executed test scope in the walkthrough.
   * **Tier 2 (Sprint Integration Gate at End of Phase 2 & Start of Ceremony 2)**: Run the full unfiltered suite `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest --max-workers=2 && python3 tools/verify_requirement_governance.py` and fix all failures as attributed commits before human review / merge.
4. **Subtask Direct Completion & Parent Human Gate (`Core Rule 3 & Rule 8`)**:
   * Passing Gate 1–5 audits close subtasks directly to `Erledigt` via `python3 tools/jira_util.py --as agent2 gate-verdict <SUBTASK_KEY> PASS "<Audit Report>"`, which synchronously advances the parent ticket to the next stage (`Test Spec` $\rightarrow$ `Implementation Plan` $\rightarrow$ `Implementation` $\rightarrow$ `Test` $\rightarrow$ `Final Review (Human)`).
   * Moving any **parent ticket** to `Erledigt` is reserved **exclusively** for the human user.
   * **`Lösungsversion` (`FixVersion`)**: Subtasks never receive a `FixVersion`. Parent tickets receive `FixVersion` only upon human acceptance during Ceremony 2 (`python3 tools/jira_util.py set-fixversion <KEY> <VERSION>`), while Stage 1–5 deliverables reference the `ACTIVE/UNRELEASED` target version reported by `python3 tools/jira_util.py versions`.

## 3. Multi-Account Jira Personas & Coordinator Governance (`ATT-1123`)
* **Agent 1 (Implementer)**: `JIRA_AGENT1_USER`, `JIRA_AGENT1_TOKEN` (`--as agent1`). Authors stage deliverables and submits stages (`submit-stage`). Comments prefixed with `[Automated comment by AI Agent 1 (Implementer)]`.
* **Agent 2 (Auditor)**: `JIRA_AGENT2_USER`, `JIRA_AGENT2_TOKEN` (`--as agent2`). Conducts independent Gate 1–5 reviews (`gate-verdict`). Comments prefixed with `[Automated comment by AI Agent 2 (Auditor)]`.
* **Coordinator (Orchestrator)**: `JIRA_COORDINATOR_USER`, `JIRA_COORDINATOR_TOKEN` (`--as coordinator`). Performs administrative orchestration, sprint tracking, and subagent dispatch. The Coordinator **cannot override** Agent 2 `CHALLENGED` or `RECOMMEND REVISION` audit verdicts, cannot bypass ASPICE gates, and **MUST NOT transition any parent ticket to `Erledigt`**.
* **Chesterton's Fence (`ATT-1141`)**: Any deliverable modifying an existing requirement in `docs/requirements.md` MUST include `### Requirement Archaeology & Chesterton's Fence Audit` with all 4 mandatory fields, verified via `python3 tools/verify_requirement_governance.py`.
* **Modular Skills (`.agents/skills/`)**: Always follow the stage- and ceremony-specific instructions in `.agents/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` (`stage1-analysis`, `stage2-req-test-spec`, `stage3-impl-plan`, `stage4-implementation`, `stage5-verification`, `jira-workflow`, `sprint-planner`, `release-manager`, `regression-bisect`, `ui-designer`, `brainstormer`).
